# Copy to .env.local for local development. Never commit the filled-in copy —
# DATABASE_URL contains your database password in plain text.

# ─── Database ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# When set, this overrides data/db-config.json and makes /settings read-only.
# Leave it unset to use the built-in SQLite file (local dev, Coolify, Railway).
#
# Use your provider's POOLED connection string on serverless hosts (Vercel).
# On Neon the pooled host contains "-pooler".
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Alternative to DATABASE_URL, if discrete values are easier to manage.
# DB_PROVIDER=postgres        # sqlite | mysql | mariadb | postgres
# DB_HOST=db.example.com
# DB_PORT=5432
# DB_NAME=content_calendar
# DB_USER=cc_user
# DB_PASSWORD=
# DB_SSL=require              # disable | require | verify

# Connections held per server instance. Serverless multiplies this by the
# number of warm instances, so keep it low. Defaults to 2 on Vercel, 5 elsewhere.
# DB_POOL_MAX=2

# ─── First-run protection ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A freshly deployed, publicly reachable instance with no accounts is claimable
# by whoever loads /login first. Set this to require a shared secret during
# admin setup. Only consulted while zero accounts exist; remove it afterwards.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 24
# SETUP_TOKEN=

# ─── AI assistant ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provider API keys are NOT set here. Each user adds their own in /settings, and
# an admin can save a shared team default there too; both are stored encrypted
# in the database. Setting ANTHROPIC_API_KEY or similar has no effect.
#
# This is the key that encrypts those stored API keys.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Required on Vercel — the filesystem is read-only there, so a key cannot be
# generated and kept. Optional elsewhere: if unset, one is created on first use
# at data/encryption.key (gitignored, mode 0600).
#
# Treat it like a database password. If it changes or is lost, every saved API
# key becomes unreadable and each user must enter theirs again. Nothing else
# breaks.
# APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# How long to wait for a model before giving up, in milliseconds. Keep this
# below your host's function timeout — 60s on Vercel unless raised in
# vercel.json. Defaults to 50000.
# LLM_TIMEOUT_MS=50000

# ─── Test mode ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A database-free trial of the app, reachable from the login screen without an
# account. The board lives in the visitor's browser tab; nothing is read from or
# written to the database, and CSV Export is the only way to keep anything.
#
# OFF unless set. It is reachable without signing in, and although it cannot
# touch your data, it does let an anonymous visitor make this server call a
# model provider they nominate — with a key they supply themselves. Enable it
# deliberately, and think twice on a public deployment.
#
# ENABLE_TEST_MODE=true
